<h2>Physics controls</h2>
<div class="presets"><button data-preset="calm">Calm</button><button data-preset="alive">Alive</button><button data-preset="energetic">Energetic</button><button data-preset="quantum">Corporate Quantum Field</button></div>
<div class="slider"><label>Central gravity <span id="gravityV" class="value"></span></label><input id="gravity" type="range" min="0" max="1.5" step=".05"></div>
<div class="slider"><label>Spring strength <span id="springV" class="value"></span></label><input id="spring" type="range" min=".005" max=".2" step=".005"></div>
<div class="slider"><label>Base spring length <span id="lengthV" class="value"></span></label><input id="length" type="range" min="80" max="400" step="10"></div>
<div class="slider"><label>Node repulsion <span id="repulsionV" class="value"></span></label><input id="repulsion" type="range" min="500" max="16000" step="250"></div>
<div class="slider"><label>Damping <span id="dampingV" class="value"></span></label><input id="damping" type="range" min=".02" max=".95" step=".01"></div>
<div class="slider"><label>Authority gravity <span id="authorityV" class="value"></span></label><input id="authority" type="range" min="0" max="3" step=".1"></div>
<div class="slider"><label>Liveliness <span id="vibrationV" class="value"></span></label><input id="vibration" type="range" min="0" max="1.5" step=".05"></div>
<div class="card" id="info"><b>Select a node</b><br>Authority is calculated from job level plus the number of known descendants beneath the position.</div>
<div class="hint">Higher-authority nodes are larger and heavier. Their connected edges are intentionally longer, giving major organizational centers more room. The field launches with physics active and receives one small initial excitation so the motion is immediately visible. Velocity and timestep remain capped. Only John and Dennis are identified, using first names only. All other employee names have been removed from both the visible graph and the embedded dataset. The star marks the President/CEO position; the hexagon marks the Technical Manager position. The red line represents the John–Dennis working relationship. This page loads vis-network from jsDelivr, so Internet access is required when opening it.</div>
